To tag on here-- even if you download ERA5 data directly through the CDS portal, the mcera5 package has some tools for processing the data so that it's curated for direct use with NicheMapR's microclimate model (as well as with a few other microclimate model toolkits, eg microclima and microclimc).

Check out the mcera5 vignette for details and a tutorial and please feel free to reach out to me with questions:
https://github.com/everydayduffy/mcera5
remotes::install_github("everydayduffy/mcera5")
ᐧ

